{"type":"message_update","usage":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":0,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"toolcall_delta","contentIndex":2,"delta":"{\"edits\":[{\"oldText\":\"def cmd_check_anchors(a):\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Every anchor must be right, and the writer's Sigstore ranges must cover entries 1..head with no gap or overlap.\\n    Checks every anchor even after a failure; exit 1 if anything was wrong, else 2 if anything couldn't be checked.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    chain, _ = load_chain(a.ledger)\\n    rows, bad, cant, ranges = [], [], [], []\\n    for path in _listdir(a.ledger, \\\"anchors\\\", ANCHOR_NAME, \\\"file in anchors\\\"):\\n        n = os.path.basename(path)\\n        m = ANCHOR_NAME.fullmatch(n)\\n        seq = int(m.group(1))\\n        try:\\n            if not 1 <= seq <= len(chain):\\n                raise Bad(f\\\"anchors/{n}: no entry {seq}\\\")\\n            raw = open(os.path.join(a.ledger, \\\"entries\\\", f\\\"{seq:06d}.json\\\"), \\\"rb\\\").read()\\n            if m.group(2) == \\\"ots\\\":\\n                t = check_ots(path, raw, a.explorer)\\n                rows.append({\\\"anchor\\\": n, \\\"kind\\\": \\\"opentimestamps\\\", \\\"existed_by\\\": iso(t) or \\\"pending\\\"})\\n            else:\\n                t, pred, commit = check_sigstore(path, chain[seq - 1][1], a.repo, a.workflow, a.ref)\\n                if not isinstance(pred, dict) or not isinstance(pred.get(\\\"from_seq\\\"), int) or pred.get(\\\"to_seq\\\") != seq \\\\\\n                        or not 1 <= pred[\\\"from_seq\\\"] <= seq or pred != range_predicate(chain, pred[\\\"from_seq\\\"], seq):\\n                    raise Bad(f\\\"anchors/{n}: attested range {pred!r} doesn't match this chain\\\")\\n                ranges.append((pred[\\\"from_seq\\\"], seq, commit))\\n                rows.append({\\\"anchor\\\": n, \\\"kind\\\": \\\"sigstore\\\", \\\"entries\\\": f\\\"{pred['from_seq']}-{seq}\\\", \\\"existed_by\\\": iso(t),\\n                             \\\"writer_commit\\\": commit})\\n        except Bad as ex:\\n            bad.append(str(ex))\\n        except CantCheck as ex:\\n            cant.append(f\\\"anchors/{n}: {ex}\\\")\\n    covered, changes, prev_commit = 0, [], None\",\"newText\":\"def cmd_check_anchors(a):\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Every anchor must be right, and the writer's Sigstore ranges must cover entries 1..head with no gap or overlap.\\n    Checks every anchor even after a failure; exit 1 if anything was wrong, else 2 if anything couldn't be checked.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    chain, _ = load_chain(a.ledger)\\n    rows, bad, cant, ranges = [], [], [], []\\n    sigstore_heads = set()  # seq numbers that have a verified Sigstore attestation\\n    for path in _listdir(a.ledger, \\\"anchors\\\", ANCHOR_NAME, \\\"file in anchors\\\"):\\n        n = os.path.basename(path)\\n        m = ANCHOR_NAME.fullmatch(n)\\n        seq = int(m.group(1))\\n        try:\\n            if not 1 <= seq <= len(chain):\\n                raise Bad(f\\\"anchors/{n}: no entry {seq}\\\")\\n            raw = open(os.path.join(a.ledger, \\\"entries\\\", f\\\"{seq:06d}.json\\\"), \\\"rb\\\").read()\\n            if m.group(2) == \\\"ots\\\":\\n                t = check_ots(path, raw, a.explorer)\\n                rows.append({\\\"anchor\\\": n, \\\"kind\\\": \\\"opentimestamps\\\", \\\"existed_by\\\": iso(t) or \\\"pending\\\"})\\n            else:\\n                t, pred, commit = check_sigstore(path, chain[seq - 1][1], a.repo, a.workflow, a.ref)\\n                if not isinstance(pred, dict) or not isinstance(pred.get(\\\"from_seq\\\"), int) or pred.get(\\\"to_seq\\\") != seq \\\\\\n                        or not 1 <= pred[\\\"from_seq\\\"] <= seq or pred != range_predicate(chain, pred[\\\"from_seq\\\"], seq):\\n                    raise Bad(f\\\"anchors/{n}: attested range {pred!r} doesn't match this chain\\\")\\n                ranges.append((pred[\\\"from_seq\\\"], seq, commit))\\n                rows.append({\\\"anchor\\\": n, \\\"kind\\\": \\\"sigstore\\\", \\\"entries\\\": f\\\"{pred['from_seq']}-{seq}\\\", \\\"existed_by\\\": iso(t),\\n                             \\\"writer_commit\\\": commit})\\n                sigstore_heads.add(seq)\\n        except Bad as ex:\\n            bad.append(str(ex))\\n        except CantCheck as ex:\\n            cant.append(f\\\"anchors/{n}: {ex}\\\")\\n    # Every Sigstore-attested range head must have an OpenTimestamps proof\\n    for seq in sorted(sigstore_heads):\\n        ots_path = os.path.join(a.ledger, \\\"anchors\\\", f\\\"{seq:06d}.ots\\\")\\n        if not os.path.exists(ots_path):\\n            bad.append(f\\\"{seq:06d}.ots is missing\\\")\\n    covered, changes, prev_commit = 0, [], None\"}],\"path\":\"/workspace/record/record.py\"}"}}
{"type":"message_update","usage":{"input":14057,"output":2289,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":953,"totalTokens":16346,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0,"totalFromProvider":true}},"assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"thinking_end","contentIndex":0,"content":"Let me understand the bug. The issue is in `cmd_check_anchors` function. Currently, it checks all anchor files in the anchors directory. For each anchor file:\n- If it's an `.ots` file, it verifies the OpenTimestamps proof\n- If it's a `.sigstore.json` file, it verifies the Sigstore attestation\n\nThe bug is that when a `.sigstore.json` file exists for a range head (e.g., `anchors/000002.sigstore.json`), there should also be a corresponding `.ots` file (e.g., `anchors/000002.ots`). If the `.ots` file is missing, the check should fail with a message like \"000002.ots is missing\".\n\nLooking at the code, `cmd_check_anchors` iterates through all anchor files found by `_listdir(a.ledger, \"anchors\", ANCHOR_NAME, \"file in anchors\")`. It processes each file individually. If there's a `.sigstore.json` file but no corresponding `.ots` file, it won't check for the missing `.ots` file because the `.ots` file simply doesn't exist in the directory listing.\n\nThe fix should be: after processing all anchors, check that for every `.sigstore.json` anchor that was successfully verified (i.e., every range head that the writer attested), there's a corresponding `.ots` file.\n\nLet me look at the code more carefully:\n\n```python\ndef cmd_check_anchors(a):\n    \"\"\"Every anchor must be right, and the writer's Sigstore ranges must cover entries 1..head with no gap or overlap.\n    Checks every anchor even after a failure; exit 1 if anything was wrong, else 2 if anything couldn't be checked.\"\"\"\n    chain, _ = load_chain(a.ledger)\n    rows, bad, cant, ranges = [], [], [], []\n    for path in _listdir(a.ledger, \"anchors\", ANCHOR_NAME, \"file in anchors\"):\n        n = os.path.basename(path)\n        m = ANCHOR_NAME.fullmatch(n)\n        seq = int(m.group(1))\n        try:\n            if not 1 <= seq <= len(chain):\n                raise Bad(f\"anchors/{n}: no entry {seq}\")\n            raw = open(os.path.join(a.ledger, \"entries\", f\"{seq:06d}.json\"), \"rb\").read()\n            if m.group(2) == \"ots\":\n                t = check_ots(path, raw, a.explorer)\n                rows.append({\"anchor\": n, \"kind\": \"opentimestamps\", \"existed_by\": iso(t) or \"pending\"})\n            else:\n                t, pred, commit = check_sigstore(path, chain[seq - 1][1], a.repo, a.workflow, a.ref)\n                if not isinstance(pred, dict) or not isinstance(pred.get(\"from_seq\"), int) or pred.get(\"to_seq\") != seq \\\n                        or not 1 <= pred[\"from_seq\"] <= seq or pred != range_predicate(chain, pred[\"from_seq\"], seq):\n                    raise Bad(f\"anchors/{n}: attested range {pred!r} doesn't match this chain\")\n                ranges.append((pred[\"from_seq\"], seq, commit))\n                rows.append({\"anchor\": n, \"kind\": \"sigstore\", \"entries\": f\"{pred['from_seq']}-{seq}\", \"existed_by\": iso(t),\n                             \"writer_commit\": commit})\n        except Bad as ex:\n            bad.append(str(ex))\n        except CantCheck as ex:\n            cant.append(f\"anchors/{n}: {ex}\")\n```\n\nSo the code processes each anchor file. For `.sigstore.json` files, it verifies the attestation and adds the range to `ranges`. For `.ots` files, it verifies the proof.\n\nThe bug is that it doesn't check that for every range head (i.e., every `seq` that appears as the `to_seq` of a verified Sigstore attestation), there's a corresponding `.ots` file.\n\nI need to:\n1. Track which sequence numbers have verified Sigstore attestations (i.e., which are range heads)\n2. After processing all anchors, check that for each such sequence number, there's a corresponding `.ots` file\n3. If not, add a \"BAD\" message like \"000002.ots is missing\"\n\nLet me implement this fix."}}
